Atlas overlay patch 0060: ui/passwords-entry
Why: with the inherited credential-saving block dropped (atlas/drop.list), a person needs a way to
reach the saved passwords: a "Passwords" item in the app menu (the engine's own command, which opens
the password page) and a "Passwords" link in the settings menu that opens the same page in a new tab,
as the extensions link does. The two labels come from chrome/app/atlas/vault_strings.grdp; the
settings label reaches the page through one loadTimeData line. A lower tier (policy, pref, flag)
cannot add a menu entry, and restoring the whole autofill settings section would bring payments,
addresses and an account store with it.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/app_menu_model.cc, chrome/browser/resources/settings/settings_menu/settings_menu.html, chrome/browser/resources/settings/settings_menu/settings_menu.ts, chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_localized_strings_provider.cc
Test filter: AppMenuModelTest.*; journey atlas-keyring (menu item opens the password page)
Rebase risk: L (a block of 8 lines in AppMenuModel::Build, one table line, one link in the settings menu)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

